QuickJS in RadiumOS
===================

Upstream: QuickJS by Fabrice Bellard and Charlie Gordon, release 2026-06-04
(see VERSION). The upstream files are kept as close to the release as
possible so a newer release can be dropped in.

Local changes to upstream files
-------------------------------
- quickjs.c: CONFIG_ATOMICS is not defined under __radiumos__ (the kernel
  has no threads for Atomics.wait/notify).

Everything else here is ours: rjs*.c / rjs*.h (embedding, DOM and canvas
bindings), dom_prelude.js (+ the generated dom_prelude.c), and compat/
(the freestanding libc, allocator and musl libm the kernel build uses).

Known sanitizer report (upstream, benign, left alone)
-----------------------------------------------------
A host build with clang >= 17 and -fsanitize=undefined (which includes
-fsanitize=function for C) reports, the first time a dynamic buffer grows or
is freed:

  cutils.c:119: runtime error: call to function js_realloc_rt through
  pointer to incorrect function type 'void *(*)(void *, void *, unsigned long)'

(also cutils.c:209 in dbuf_free.) The cause is upstream's

  dbuf_init2(s, ctx->rt, (DynBufReallocFunc *)js_realloc_rt);

in js_dbuf_init and js_string_normalize (quickjs.c): js_realloc_rt takes a
JSRuntime * where DynBufReallocFunc takes a void *. The call is formally
undefined in ISO C, but both are plain data pointers passed identically by
every ABI QuickJS targets (i386 cdecl included), the RadiumOS kernel is not
built with control-flow integrity, and upstream has carried the cast for
years. It is not a bug in our code; none of rjs*.c casts function pointers.

To keep the host test runs quiet without patching upstream, compile cutils.c
(the call site) without that one check, e.g.

  clang ... -fno-sanitize=function -c src/quickjs/cutils.c

With that, tools/rbrowse/test_js.c and test_canvas.c run clean under
-fsanitize=address,undefined (Homebrew clang 22, 2026-11). Apple clang 21
does not enable the check for C and reports nothing.
